# Agents the Ralph runners may use. Copy this file to `agents` (ignored by Git) and edit the copy.
#
# Format, one agent per line: stage|agent|model|effort
#   stage   worker: `ralph`, `ralph-afk` and the `ralph-afk --pr` workers.
#           reviewer: the `ralph-afk --pr` reviewers only; sequential mode ignores these lines.
#           merger: the `ralph-afk --pr` agent that merges the base into a conflicting approved PR. Without merger lines
#           the worker lines do it. Sequential mode ignores these lines.
#   agent   claude or codex. Each has a built-in probe (bin/ralph-probe.mjs) that also reports when a usage limit resets.
#   model   Work model, passed as --model.
#   effort  Reasoning effort for --pr agents; - keeps the CLI default. `ralph` and `ralph-afk` ignore it.
#
# In --pr mode, line order within a stage is the fallback order.
# The schedule setting decides which agents may run in each hour; comment a line out to stop using that agent.
# reviewer|human: you review --pr PRs on GitHub: merge to accept, comment to have the worker fix them.
#   The other reviewer lines are then ignored. Sequential mode ignores it.
# reviewer|none: no review; --pr squash-merges each PR once its CI passes. The merger merges the base into a conflicting one first.
#   The other reviewer lines are then ignored. Not together with worker|human.
# worker|human: you write the code on a branch named after the task and open the PR; --pr only reviews it.
#   No worker agent runs. Sequential mode ignores it. Not together with reviewer|human.
#
# Settings, one line each as name|value; a missing one keeps the default shown. The --pr dashboard edits them and
# the lines above with s, and a running --pr applies a saved change to the next agent it starts.
#   workers|3                      --pr workers at once. Sequential mode ignores it.
#   reviewers|2                    --pr reviewers at once. Sequential mode ignores it.
#   tries|3                        --pr: failed agent runs on one task or PR before it is labelled needs-human.
#   slow-every|5                   --pr: merges between runs of the slow-test workflow on GitHub.
#   schedule|00-24=claude,codex    Space-separated FROM-TO=agents windows in local hours; agents are tried in order.
#                                  An hour outside every window runs nothing.
#   wait|600                       Seconds before probing again an agent that gave no reset time.
#   poll|120                       Seconds between --pr checks for new tasks and PR changes.

worker|claude|sonnet|high
worker|codex|gpt-6.2-sol|medium
reviewer|claude|opus|high
merger|claude|sonnet|medium
